1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:15,000
PawTwin helps family members continue caring for the same pet.
This is a local prototype with a labelled Alexa web simulation.

2
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:35,000
Each member has an independent local account and shares one household record.
A family label such as Dad does not change that member's permissions.

3
00:00:35,000 --> 00:01:05,000
These are fictional demonstration measurements: 1.20 and 1.35 kilograms.
The program calculates 150 grams, 12.5 percent, across seven actual days.
The report exposes source records. Missing food intake stays unrecorded.

4
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:35,000
A candidate preference is excluded until the owner confirms it.
The other member signs out and signs back in, then asks through the Alexa simulator.
The new local-rule answer cites the confirmed record. No cloud model was called.

5
00:01:35,000 --> 00:02:10,000
The owner chooses a play-care type, title and time, then confirms the proposal.
Only confirmation creates the manual task. Another member claims and completes it.
The authenticated completing actor is recorded separately from the assigned member.

6
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:40,000
Today's report counts the completed manual care.
The owner deletes the preference. A fresh answer no longer cites that record.
Earlier answers remain historical. Care completion does not mean a device dispensed food.

7
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:55,000
Shared records, traceable statistics and confirmed care work locally.
Live AI planning, household cloud storage and real Alexa remain unfinished.
The source and English testing guide explain exactly what can be reproduced.
